County","/arc-plc/illinois/hancock-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids. June to July, August to September and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of those years. In 2025 on the middle, August to September came in at 31% of normal and January to February at 25%. Grid 24154 had its driest year in 1988 at 53%.</p>"}
